 "Utilities": "公用事业",
 "US ~$2,000 incl. federal, state and local": "美国约 $2,000（含联邦、州和地方）",
 "Spring rains flood riverside homes and tornadoes tear through a few blocks; FEMA pays $750 to each household hit. Summer heat waves hurt health, most of all for the old and very young.": "春雨淹没河边住宅，龙卷风横扫几个街区；FEMA 给每户受灾家庭 $750。夏季热浪损害健康，对老人和幼儿最严重。",
 "Each law is a real lever in the engine: tax rates, the minimum wage on every job, city cash assistance and basic income paid each month, how many police officers, teachers, nurses and doctors the city employs, how drug users are treated, college tuition, whether employers may check records, affirmative action, whether the town is dry, the gas tax and the sales tax.": "每条法律都是引擎中的真实杠杆：税率、每份工作的最低工资、每月发放的城市现金援助和基本收入、城市雇用多少警员、教师、护士和医生、如何对待吸毒者、大学学费、雇主能否查前科、平权措施、小镇是否禁酒、燃油税和销售税。",
 "Taxes follow the US and Ohio: federal income tax (10-37% above the $16,100 standard deduction), FICA (7.65% from workers and employers), Ohio income tax (2.75% above $26,050), a 2% city income tax, 7.25% sales tax with groceries exempt, property tax through rents, 21% corporate tax and the federal estate tax above $15M. Low earners get the EITC and the Child Tax Credit back with their tax return.": "税收依照美国和俄亥俄州：联邦所得税（超过 $16,100 标准扣除额部分 10-37%）、FICA（工人和雇主各 7.65%）、俄亥俄州所得税（超过 $26,050 部分 2.75%）、2% 城市所得税、食品免税的 7.25% 销售税、通过租金体现的房产税、21% 公司税，以及超过 $15M 的联邦遗产税。低收入者通过报税取回 EITC 和儿童税收抵免。",
 "The Fed sets the federal funds rate (3.75-4.00% in late 2026); the town economy moves it between 0.25% and 6%.": "美联储设定联邦基金利率（2026 年底为 3.75-4.00%）；小镇经济让它在 0.25% 到 6% 之间变动。",
