 "National laws (income tax, company tax, VAT, social insurance) are set in Beijing. The city sets the minimum wage class, hardship aid, police, teachers, nurses and doctors, how drug users are treated, university fees, record checks, hiring preference, alcohol and fuel help.": "国家法律（所得税、公司税、增值税、社会保险）由北京制定。城市制定最低工资档次、困难救助、警察、教师、护士和医生、如何对待吸毒者、大学学费、前科审查、招聘优先、酒类和燃油补助。",
 "Taxes follow China: individual income tax (3-45% above ¥60,000 a year, ¥2,000 a month per child), social insurance (10.5% from workers, ~25% from employers, between 60% and 300% of the average wage), the Housing Provident Fund (7% + 7%), VAT 13% (food 9%, services 6%) inside prices, property tax on business premises only, 25% company tax (5% for small firms) and 10% on dividends.": "税收依照中国：个人所得税（超过每年 ¥60,000 部分 3-45%，每个孩子每月扣除 ¥2,000）、社会保险（工人 10.5%，雇主约 25%，按平均工资的 60% 到 300% 计算）、住房公积金（7% + 7%）、含在价格中的 13% 增值税（食品 9%，服务 6%）、只对经营场所征收的房产税、25% 企业所得税（小微企业 5%）和 10% 股息税。",
